5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005140-Strumpf1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Strumpf</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsang</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>Sayre</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><year>1979</year><article-title>Re-evaluation of sputum staining for the diagnosis of pulmonary tuberculosis.</article-title><source>Am Rev Respir Dis</source><volume>119(4)</volume><fpage>599</fpage><lpage>602</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">87141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005140-Bell1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dacombe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Graham</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hicks</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Simple measures are as effective as invasive techniques in the diagnosis of pulmonary tuberculosis in Malawi.</article-title><source>Int J Tuberc Lung Dis</source><volume>13(1)</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19105886</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005140-Saglam1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saglam</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Akgun</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Aktas</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Usefulness of induced sputum and fibreoptic bronchoscopy specimens in the diagnosis of pulmonary tuberculosis.</article-title><source>J Int Med Res</source><volume>33(2)</volume><fpage>260</fpage><lpage>5</l